        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "aa18e252-e514-35e2-99ae-c13c69011dc1",
                "word": "lork",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b036483c-0773-4dba-8ef8-7362ad5e22e0",
                        "entry_id": "aa18e252-e514-35e2-99ae-c13c69011dc1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lorken"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "130f4ca1-6262-3b9a-b079-9fbffd095858",
                        "entry_id": "aa18e252-e514-35e2-99ae-c13c69011dc1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "benaming voor naaldbomen uit het geslacht Larix die in de winter hun naalden laten vallen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "coniferen"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5209392c-9f2e-4842-95ee-d29f7fd68591",
                                "sense_id": "130f4ca1-6262-3b9a-b079-9fbffd095858",
                                "text": "‘Je ziet het overal in Vlaanderen: toppen van naaldbomen die ros staan te blinken in de zon. Voor een fijnspar kan dat duiden op aantasting, terwijl dat voor een lork net een teken van een goede gezondheid is. Verwarrend, dus best even dubbelchecken.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8db85d76-9492-4e98-a29d-8ffd2210d8f0",
                                "sense_id": "130f4ca1-6262-3b9a-b079-9fbffd095858",
                                "text": "De Bourgoyen-Ossemeersen staat internationaal bekend voor zijn open graslanden. Die trekken zeer veel watervogels aan. Maar midden in het natuurreservaat, vlak bij de R4, ligt een vreemde eend in de bijt: het Valkenhuisbos. Dat is tien voetbalvelden groot en telt zowat 700 sparren, dennen, lorken en populieren. Stuk voor stuk buitenlandse soorten, en deze zomer worden ze allemaal gekapt."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "09c9efcf-b5e3-47db-aef5-fdefc4f799ae",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa18e252-e514-35e2-99ae-c13c69011dc1",
                        "source_sense_id": "130f4ca1-6262-3b9a-b079-9fbffd095858",
                        "source_sense_description": "benaming voor naaldbomen uit het geslacht Larix",
                        "target_lang_word": "larch",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "larch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                        "entry_id": "4e4ead3e-840a-3780-9bb4-4f77cb8e17a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coniferous tree, of genus Larix, having deciduous leaves, in fascicles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f6460e1-793b-4f56-b329-06a038ac2b2f",
                                                "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                                "text": "The Larch-tree, with us, groweth slowly, and to be found in few places; it hath a rugged bark, and boughts that branch in good order, with divers small yellowish bunched eminences, set thereon at several distances, from whence tufts of many small, long, and narrow smooth leaves do yearly come forth; it beareth among the green leaves many beautiful flowers, which are of a fine crimson colour […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "156cde97-26fd-43f8-b212-03bbbb0acf8f",
                                                "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                                "text": "1716, Nicholas Rowe (translator), The Ninth Book of Lucan in John Dryden, Miscellany Poems, London: Jacob Tonson, Volume 6, p. 67,\nThe Gummy Larch-Tree, and the Thapsos there,\nWound-wort and Maiden-weed, perfume the Air."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c99ff38b-cd3d-4c45-b0ec-198ea485e099",
                                                "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                                "text": "Thus the Birch Canoe was builded\nIn the valley, by the river,\nIn the bosom of the forest;\nAnd the forest’s life was in it,\nAll its mystery and its magic,\nAll the lightness of the birch-tree,\nAll the toughness of the cedar,\nAll the larch’s supple sinews;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ef6e91c-ed37-4fb7-b3af-1eef37ca07c9",
                                                "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                                "text": "Joan was thinking: ‘She looks like a tree […] it must be the green dress. But her eyes are like water, all greeny and shadowy and deep looking—a tree near a pool, that’s what she’s like, a tall tree. A beech tree? No, that’s too spready—a larch tree, that’s Elizabeth; a larch tree just greening over.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebdd7a36-b529-48d9-b2bb-12d92de84ec7",
                                                "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                                "text": "Have a tree or two the witches particularly like, such as the alder, larch, cypress and hemlock; then, to counteract any possible evil effects, there must be a holly, yew, hazel, elder, mountain ash or juniper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f9a6fc9-e7db-470e-b741-a7fd2460165d",
                                                "sense_id": "56b4ecf7-6b6d-3edb-ad0d-6d42b494677a",
                                                "text": "During the early 1980s to early 1990s, and especially in the long drought period of 1982-3, extensive fires swept through natural forests in many parts of the world. While the ravaging fires in Australia and Europe received wide media coverage, 1 million hectares of larch forests were wiped out on the Ta-hsing-an-ling mountain in north-eastern China (H. Tagawa, personal communication)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "045f258b-4d98-3bab-b539-673a9f6386a3",
                                        "entry_id": "4e4ead3e-840a-3780-9bb4-4f77cb8e17a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wood of the larch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc8b912-0268-4f00-aa52-45dc0e93c2b9",
                                                "sense_id": "045f258b-4d98-3bab-b539-673a9f6386a3",
                                                "text": "Old Peter was up early too, harnessing the little yellow horse into the old cart. The cart was of rough wood, without springs, like a big box fixed on long larch poles between two pairs of wheels. The larch poles did instead of springs, bending and creaking, as the cart moved over the forest track."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
